---
/**
 * Rest Reminder tool page.
 */
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import RestReminder from '../../components/tools/RestReminder';
---

<ToolLayout slug="rest-reminder">
  <RestReminder client:load />

  <Fragment slot="about">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">01 · Fires while minimised</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A <code class="text-accent font-mono">requestAnimationFrame</code> countdown stops dead when
          the window goes down. Every phase here is an absolute deadline, armed three ways: one long
          <code class="text-accent font-mono">setTimeout</code>, a 1s reconciliation interval, and
          visibility listeners.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          A deadline missed during sleep is caught up, not skipped.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">02 · Every cycle alerts</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Notifications coalesce by <code class="text-accent font-mono">tag</code>, so a fixed tag
          makes the second alert silently replace the first: one banner, then apparent silence. Each
          alert now carries its own tag and sets
          <code class="text-accent font-mono">renotify</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Delivery panel shows which link in the chain is broken.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">03 · No chime</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The alert is the OS banner, the card at the top of this page, and the tab title. The one
          audio node is a 30 Hz tone at a gain of 0.0015, inaudible, held open only while a phase
          runs so the browser counts the tab as playing audio and leaves its timers alone.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Cadence and history stay in this browser's local storage.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hud-card border-warn mt-6 border-l-2 p-5">
      <h3 class="eyebrow text-warn mb-3">Limits worth knowing</h3>
      <ul class="text-muted grid gap-3 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span>
            <strong>The tab stays open.</strong> Firing from a closed tab needs a push server, which this
            site does not have. Minimised is fine.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span>
            <strong>The OS gets the last word.</strong> Windows Focus Assist and macOS Focus swallow granted
            notifications silently. The delivery panel has a ten second test for that.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span>
            <strong>The carrier needs one click.</strong> Autoplay policy refuses an audio context opened
            inside a timer callback, so starting a block opens it. Until then the tab is throttleable.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span>
            <strong>20-20-20.</strong> Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds.
            That is the eye-care preset; the 90 minute one follows the ultradian cycle instead.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
